<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aristocratic Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aristocratic Republic is the name given by the historian Jorge Basadre to the period of Peruvian history from 1895 to 1919, when governments dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civilista-party">Civilista Party</a> and the coastal landowning and financial oligarchy ruled through regular, restricted elections. It brought relative stability, export growth in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, minerals and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, and the modernisation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>. It ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-b-leguia">Augusto B. Leguía</a>'s coup of 1919.</p></div>
